>> title: Gumbo
>> category: Soups
>> tags: chicken, sausage, shrimp, okra, creole, one-pot
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: chicken and sausage gumbo, seafood gumbo, gumbo ya-ya, Louisiana gumbo
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — thirty-five minutes of stirring flour and oil to milk chocolate, without stopping, and there is no way to hurry it that does not end in scorched flour and a pot to start again; the trinity going in is what stops the roux, and it goes in on time or not at all
>> step.1: The roux is made in the gumbo pot, which is the reason this is one pot at all. Thirty-five minutes of flour and oil over medium heat, stirred without stopping, taken to the colour of milk chocolate — that is the whole difference between gumbo and soup, and there is no way to hurry it that does not end in scorched flour and a pot to start again.
>> step.2: brown 8 min, out to a plate
>> step.3: stir the roux 35 min, to milk chocolate
>> step.4: sweat the trinity 6 min — the roux stops here
>> step.5: simmer 45 min, shred the chicken in
>> step.6: simmer 8 min, sausage back, filé off the heat
>> step.7: A bowl of gumbo is dinner as it stands. Rice under it is how most people eat it and it is a second pot, so it is your call and not the recipe's — the pot is finished without it. Filé goes in off the heat or it turns the whole thing stringy.

The roux is made in the gumbo pot, which is the reason this is one pot at all. Thirty-five minutes of flour and oil over medium heat, stirred without stopping, taken to the colour of milk chocolate — that is the whole difference between gumbo and soup, and there is no way to hurry it that does not end in scorched flour and a pot to start again.

Brown @andouille sausage{12%oz}(340 g; sliced in coins) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{8%min}, then out to a plate.

Stir @vegetable oil{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g) over medium heat for ~stir{35%min}, without stopping, until it is the colour of milk chocolate.

Soften @&(~1)dark roux{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @celery{3%ribs}(diced), @green bell pepper{1%large}(diced), @garlic{5%cloves}(minced) for ~saute{6%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)trinity{} with @chicken stock{8%cups}(1.9 L), @bone-in chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(700 g), @bay leaves{2}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} for ~simmer{45%min}, then pull the chicken, shred it and put it back.

Simmer @&(~1)gumbo{} with @&(~4)browned sausage{}, @okra{8%oz}(225 g; sliced), @large shrimp{1%lb}(450 g; peeled), @scallions{4}(sliced), @filé powder{1%tsp}(off the heat) for ~simmer{8%min}.

A bowl of gumbo is dinner as it stands. Rice under it is how most people eat it and it is a second pot, so it is your call and not the recipe's — the pot is finished without it. Filé goes in off the heat or it turns the whole thing stringy.
